eaves the other fixed at its prior.\n\nI'm checking whether, under A-FDT, holding F_y fixed at its prior makes defecting dominate for both copies, so the unique fixed point is mutual defection. I'm also weighing whether the input difference is irrelevant enough to treat the copies as one computation, but the essay treats different-input copies as separate nodes, so I'll go with defecting and submitting the letter.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through a twin prisoner's dilemma where each copy sees different information, so under A-FDT my node is F_x and the other copy's is F_y, and I'm checking whether intervening on one actually leaves the other fixed at its prior.\n\nI'm checking whether, under A-FDT, holding F_y fixed at its prior makes defecting dominate for both copies, so the unique fixed point is mutual defection. I'm also weighing whether the input difference is irrelevant enough to treat the copies as one computation, but the essay treats different-input copies as separate nodes, so I'll go with defecting and submitting the letter.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10055,"completion_tokens":945,"total_tokens":11000,"cost":0.05912,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.05912,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.04022,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0189},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":465,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}